{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-27366","model_call":42,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"history of minimalism\" \"abstract expressionism\")"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"history of minimalism\" \"abstract expressionism\")"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_755431544#4_1565564818","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q2428","rank":1,"snippet":": \"History of Minimalism: How the Minimalist Movement Happened History of Minimalism: How the Minimalist Movement Happened Minimalist Design A Brief History of Minimalism Here are a few highlights from the past 200 years: 1800-1850: Introducing Simple Living in America 1920-1930: The Elevated Design Era 1960-1970: Minimalist Expansion 1980-2000: Adaptation of Simple Living 2000 – Present: Minimalism Becomes Mainstream Important Figures in the Minimalist Movement Donald Judd Carl Andre Dan Flavin Summary of the <cover>History of Minimalism Exclusive Member of Mediavine Home \" , \"segment\": \"Minimalism started being used as a colloquial term in writing, painting, architecture, and other aesthetic, design, and creative fields. Minimalists started to break off from the Abstract Expressionism </cover>of previous generations, removing the storytelling or metaphors from their art and focusing on industrial materials, white space, and sleek, simplistic works. Moreover, in the 70s Dieter Rams introduced his principles of good design and ever since has been praised as one of the most influential figures in the pared back, user-friendly product design trend that’s so commonly called minimalist design. 1980-2000: Adaptation of Simple Living The next stage of the history of minimalism saw an "},"time":53},"model_calls":42,"document_judgments":34,"relevance_3":10,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
