{"actor":"model","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-27366","model_call":43,"attempt":1,"model":"gpt-5.5","usage":{"input_tokens":21069,"output_tokens":269,"total_tokens":21338,"cached_tokens":20224,"reasoning_tokens":56},"output_characters":1003,"decision":{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_755431544#4_1565564818","relevance":3,"reason":"The document is dedicated to the history of Minimalism and directly explains its development: Minimalism became used in writing, painting, architecture, design, and creative fields, and Minimalists broke off from Abstract Expressionism by removing storytelling/metaphor and focusing on industrial materials, white space, and simplicity. This directly supports an answer about whether Minimalism comes from creativity by identifying its art/design historical sources and creative fields.","learned":"A history-of-Minimalism source says Minimalism arose across aesthetic, design, and creative fields and developed partly by breaking from Abstract Expressionism toward industrial materials, white space, and simplified works."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q2428","reason":"This query produced a dedicated history-of-Minimalism result with direct evidence; continue to find more grade-3 historical sources."}}}
